WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
Start with a single cell from your body.

2
00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:06.490
It is about ten to the
minus five metres across.

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.170
Now zoom out.

4
00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.840
Past a person, past a
city, past the Earth,

5
00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:13.910
to the edge of our galaxy.

6
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:18.000
The Milky Way is about ten to
the twenty-one metres across.

7
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:21.890
Line up cells side by side,
from one edge to the other.

8
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.340
How many would you need?

9
00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.260
A billion?

10
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:25.530
Far more?

11
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:30.240
In this mission, you'll write huge
and tiny numbers in standard form:

12
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:34.280
a times ten to the k, with
a between one and ten.

13
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:38.860
And you'll calculate with powers of
ten: multiplying adds the indices,

14
00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:40.840
dividing subtracts them.

15
00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:46.110
Your mission: work out how many cells
laid end to end would cross the Milky Way.
